# cerebro-unlanded.service — oneshot un-ingested-report sweep, fired hourly by
# cerebro-unlanded.timer. Read-only: it classifies every finished X-Man report,
# maintains ~/.cerebro/logs/unlanded-register, and nudges the coordinator ONLY
# when the unlanded set changes. It never writes the vault, never ingests, and
# never commits — landing a finding stays with /ingest, which is judgment.
#
# WHY A TIMER AND NOT A CRON. The `crons:` entries in the scheduled-tasks-log are
# CronCreate jobs that live inside a Claude Code host session: they do not
# survive /clear, /exit, or a restart, which is the whole reason /rearm-crons
# exists. This sweep's requirement is that it runs without anyone remembering to
# — a session-scoped job cannot meet that, and the prose rule it replaces failed
# in exactly that way (it only ran when a fleet tick remembered it, and each
# fresh-context tick started from the uncorrected version). A user timer with
# linger survives logout and reboot.
#
# Install:
#   cp scripts/cerebro/systemd/cerebro-unlanded.{service,timer} ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user enable --now cerebro-unlanded.timer
#   loginctl enable-linger kyle   # survive logout/reboot
[Unit]
Description=Cerebro un-ingested report sweep (detect only, never lands)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/vault/scripts/cerebro/cb-unlanded --tick
